\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Distinguished zero-area smooth images from positive-area closures and constructed kinematic dense bands of area pi a. No Newtonian shape realization, limit-cycle theorem or component classification.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the supplied complete definition, catalogue wording, scope qualifications and source list for this canonical ID. The original-source citations are inherited as supplied references; no fresh primary-source or novelty search was performed for this attempt. No current open-status claim is inferred from this calculation.

\paragraph{Smooth image versus closure area.}A smooth curve on a two-dimensional sphere has area zero on every compact time interval: in a coordinate chart its Lipschitz image can be covered by \(O(1/\delta)\) squares of side \(O(\delta)\), giving total area \(O(\delta)\). A countable union over bounded intervals still has zero area. This does not imply that its closure has zero area, which is the actual source target.
\paragraph{An explicit kinematic dense-band example.}On a sphere of radius \(1/2\), whose total area is \(\pi\), use coordinates \(\theta\pmod{2\pi}\) and normalized height \(z\in[-1,1]\). The curve \(\theta(t)=t\pmod{2\pi}\), \(z(t)=a\sin(\sqrt2t)\), \(0<a<1\), is smooth and dense in the band \(|z|\le a\). To verify density, times \(t=\theta_0+2\pi n+o(1)\) reduce the second phase to an irrational circle rotation; its orbit is dense, as follows by the pigeonhole approximation of a nonzero arbitrarily small rotation step and its multiples. The area element is \(\tfrac14d\theta\,dz\), so the closure has area \(\pi a\). These curves are kinematic examples, not three-body shape trajectories.
\paragraph{Gap.}Thus no purely dimension-of-a-curve argument refutes the requested positive closure areas. Conversely the ability to draw a dense curve gives no Newtonian realization. One must construct a physical invariant set or orbit whose projected closure has the specified area, while controlling collisions and conserved quantities. Shape-space limit cycles and connected components of closed realizable shape curves are also unproved; homotopy through arbitrary curves does not supply a deformation through solutions. The first missing step is a dynamical realization with a specified topology and reconstruction condition.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked image-area covering, sphere area normalization, irrational-phase density, band area and explicit non-dynamical status of the example. This was an LLM adversarial audit, not independent human verification; no theorem prover was used. Prompts A then B applied to this ID: Checked image-area covering, sphere area normalization, irrational-phase density, band area and explicit non-dynamical status of the example. Scope remains limited: Construct actual three-body invariant sets/orbits realizing the desired closure geometry and reconstruction conditions.

Coordinator checked the irrational-flow density argument and area of the latitude band on the radius-one-half sphere; the example is kinematic. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

